[32;1m[1;3mQuestion: A fund manager holds a portfolio of 6 assets and is considering using 120 European option types for hedging. Each option’s per-contract cost, delta, gamma, vega, and trading limits are given in OptionCharacteristics.csv. The underlying asset(s) each option refers to are given in Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv, with A[i,j]=1 if option i references asset j and 0 otherwise. (Note: some options may reference more than one asset.)

Variables:
Let x_i be the integer number of contracts (positive for buy/long, negative for sell/short) for option i, i=1,...,120.

Objective:
Minimize total hedging cost:
\min \sum_{i=1}^{120} \text{Cost}[i] \cdot |x_i|

Subject to:

For each Greek G ∈ {Δ,Γ,Vega}, the net portfolio exposure after hedging must satisfy:
\bigg| G_{\text{initial}} + \sum_{i=1}^{120} \sum_{j=1}^{6} G[i] \cdot A[i,j] \cdot x_i \bigg| \leq \text{Tolerance}_G

Where:
• G_{\text{initial}} is the initial exposure for that Greek (given).
• G[i] is the per-contract Greek exposure of option i (from OptionCharacteristics.csv).
• A[i,j] is from Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv.
• \text{Tolerance}_G is the band for each risk metric (given).

Trading limits:
\text{MaxShort}[i] \leq x_i \leq \text{MaxLong}[i],   i=1,...,120

Data provided:
• OptionCharacteristics.csv: Option, Cost, Delta, Gamma, Vega, MaxLong, MaxShort
• Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv: binary matrix (120 × 6) showing which option references which asset (A[i,j])
• Initial net Delta = 0.25, Gamma = 0.08, Vega = 0.17
• Risk band tolerances: |\Delta| ≤ 0.06, |\Gamma| ≤ 0.05, |\text{Vega}| ≤ 0.07

Task:
Find the optimal integer positions x_i, i=1,...,120 that minimize total hedging cost, such that all risk exposures after hedging are within their respective bands, while respecting per-option trading limits and using the asset-reference information in the constraints.

Thought: I need to retrieve all option characteristics (cost, delta, gamma, vega, max long, max short) for all 120 options from OptionCharacteristics.csv, and the full 120×6 binary matrix from Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv. I will preserve all identifiers and values. I will then use the initial exposures and tolerances as given.

Action: CSVQA
Action Input: Retrieve all rows and columns from OptionCharacteristics.csv and Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv, preserving all identifiers and values.
